cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "AgriSentinel: An Explainable Early-Warning System for National Food-Security Risk"
message: "If you use this software or its results, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: "Soe Sett"
    family-names: "Lynn"
    affiliation: "University of Computer Studies (Yangon)"
repository-code: "https://github.com/ssettlynn/AgriSentinel"
url: "https://predictagrisentinel.netlify.app/"
abstract: >-
  AgriSentinel classifies every country into a Low / Medium / High food-security
  risk tier at one-year and five-year horizons, and explains each prediction with
  SHAP. It combines FAOSTAT food-security indicators with World Bank economic
  indicators for 180 countries over 2010-2023, using a strictly chronological
  train / validation / test split so no future information can leak into the past.
  Because a missed High-risk country costs more than a false alarm, models are
  compared on the F-beta score (beta = 2) alongside macro-F1, and the
  misclassification cost is varied explicitly through a class-weight sweep.
keywords:
  - food security
  - early warning
  - explainable machine learning
  - SHAP
  - FAOSTAT
  - World Bank
  - data mining
license: MIT
version: "1.1.0"
date-released: "2026-09-20"
